From 869657ccb25d988e94211c87f1a1323618ca673f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xuxh1 <18172956238@163.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:52:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hydrology): floodplain water re-infiltrates into the
 soil of flooded soil patches (Q-43)

DEF_FLOODPLAIN_INFILTRATION (default off): the grid-based routing publishes
flood fraction and depth to the patches; WATER_VSF offers the flood depth
of the flooded part to the runoff scheme as the CaMa-Flood LWINFILT block
does, the infiltrated part enters the soil (not the surface runoff) and
lowers the local flood depth, and the routing takes the infiltrated water
out of its storage at the next routing step. The patch and solver water
balances count it; the master logs the yearly total with the floodplain
evaporation. New module MOD_FloodInfiltration holds the patch arrays.

